# The repo root holds only stow packages, so ignore everything at the root and
# re-include the packages explicitly. A new top-level directory has to be
# whitelisted here before it is tracked, which is deliberate.
/*
/*/
!.gitignore
!README.md
!common/
!gui/
!laptop/
!x11/
!wayland/

# Never track worktrees.
.worktrees/

# Secrets, caches and generated state living inside the mirrored trees. These
# are unanchored (**/) so they apply inside whichever package holds the file,
# and keep applying if a file is moved between packages.
**/.config/gh/hosts.yml
**/.config/git/hosts.yml
**/.config/github-copilot
**/.config/github-copilot/hosts.json
**/.config/ok
**/.config/ok/auth_refresh
**/.config/ok/cacert.pem
**/.config/.env
**/.config/trmnlp/config.yml
**/.config/pulse/cookie
**/.config/Bitwarden CLI/**

# Generated or machine-local state.
**/.config/btop/btop.log
**/.config/newsboat/urls
**/.config/switchboard/history.json
**/.config/dconf/user
**/.config/QtProject.conf
**/.config/RStudio/desktop.ini
**/.config/fcitx/dbus/
**/.config/fcitx5/conf/cached_layouts
**/.config/nvim/spell/*.spl
**/.config/systemd/user/default.target.wants
**/.config/systemd/user/timers.target.wants
**/.config/background/*jen*

# Applications that manage their own large config trees.
**/.config/calibre
**/.config/obsidian/**
**/.config/libreoffice/**
**/.config/obs-studio
**/.config/vifm/**
**/.config/go/**
**/.config/claude/**
**/.claude
**/.config/chromium
**/.config/ibus*
**/.config/jobfeed
**/.config/geonote/
**/.config/inkscape
**/.config/digest-downloads
**/.config/BraveSoftware
**/.config/google-chrome
**/.config/google-chrome-headless
**/.config/microsoft-edge
**/.config/opera
**/.config/vivaldi
**/Tools/**
